# TT.TICKET_INTERFACE -- the package's two FUNCTIONs: get_next_recent_ticket (S-TICKET-033:
# MIN(id) over open, non-deferred tickets above p_last_ticket_id with optional host / type /
# resolve-age filters, p_host_id = 0 meaning "host IS NULL"; never raises) and
# replace_id_placeholders (S-TICKET-037: ##ticket_id## / ##event_id## substitution, no
# database access). Results are recorded in diff_probe.n / .s and compared directly.
#
# The ticket population is fixture-only on both sides (tt.ticket is empty in the Oracle
# container and in the PostgreSQL template, checked 2026-10-21); every get_next_recent_ticket
# call is additionally scoped by the fixture host 954075 or by p_host_id = 0 + a fixture-only
# ticket type, so a future non-empty tt.ticket cannot leak into the result.
#
# ORA_USER=system: the fixtures insert into stop.company, stop.contact and mss.host.
ORA_USER=system
COMMITS=no
COMPARE_MSG=no
DESCRIPTION=get_next_recent_ticket over tickets 954080-954086 (status/host/type/resolve-age filters) and replace_id_placeholders edge cases
